# Adoption of Libvirt's Modular Architecture in Solus
# Solus has successfully adopted libvirt's modern modular architecture. This transition replaces the traditional monolithic libvirtd daemon with specialized daemons, enhancing security and resource management.
#
# Benefits of the Modular Architecture
# Improved Security: Each daemon operates independently, reducing the risk of a single point of failure and enhancing overall system security.
# Resource Management: The modular approach allows for running only the necessary components, optimizing resource usage.
# Key Daemons in the Modular Architecture
# Daemon Name	Functionality
# virtqemud	Manages QEMU/KVM virtual machines
# virtnetworkd	Handles virtual network management
# virtstoraged	Manages storage pools and volumes
# virtnodedevd	Manages node devices (e.g., PCI, USB)
# virtproxyd	Provides remote access and compatibility with legacy clients
# Conclusion
# The shift to a modular architecture in Solus not only enhances security and resource management but also aligns with modern virtualization practices, ensuring a more robust and efficient environment for users.
